# A place the code defines when it runs (`x: int: 4`, the int place by the written int contract) holds an int: the
# application x(1; 2) -- the call mark of P0 -- finds no callable there and is refused when the code runs (5). Before M6
# (slice 344, the author 2026-11-09: only f(args) calls) x(1; 2) was the tree of `x: 1 2`, a write with two values (2).
# The fixture wrote `x: 4` until slice 347: with x unknown that is the Structure x with the content 4 (Codex
# CODEX-OPUS-347-4C-READER-REPLY-20261110T072610Z-01), not an int place; the graph's root still defines an int place
# from it -- an open boundary of the root reading.
x: int: 4
x(1; 2)
int: y x
